# What is Rocci?

Rocci is a set of deliberately small layers for building interfaces with Roc.
It adds author-friendly syntax where Roc is intentionally general, then lowers
that syntax back to ordinary Roc and web-platform primitives.

## The four pieces

### Rocci templates

A `.rocci` module is mostly Roc. `@component` marks the regions that use a
bounded HTML template grammar. The compiler lowers those regions to calls such
as `Html.element`, `Html.attribute`, and `Html.text`.

Use Rocci templates for components, complete pages, server-rendered fragments,
and views in a Roc application.

### Rocdown documents

A `.rocdown` file is mostly Markdown. Document-root declarations such as
`@page`, `@roc`, `@component`, and `@render` make executable or structural
regions explicit. Code fences are always documentation.

Use Rocdown for guides, articles, documentation, and content-heavy pages that
may need a small amount of Roc-native behavior.

### The runtime

`rocci run` compiles a standalone `.rocci` or `.rocdown` file, or a directory
with an authored `main.roc`. It serves the app over local HTTP and can open it
inside a native Tao/Wry window. The same URL works in an ordinary browser.

### Rocdown sites and knowledge

Rocdown includes a static site generator and Open Knowledge Format tooling
(`rocdown`). Rust owns discovery, routes, the content catalog, and Markdown
rendering. A Rocdown theme owns the visible site shell. This split keeps
content builds deterministic without asking the Roc compiler to type-check prose.

## What Rocci is not

- It is not JSX embedded throughout Roc.
- It is not a client-side application framework.
- It does not execute fenced code blocks.
- It does not hide HTTP or HTML behind a proprietary UI runtime.
- It does not type-check Roc; generated programs still go through the Roc compiler.

## Where it fits

Choose Rocci when you want the guarantees and data modeling of Roc, but you
also want to author semantic HTML directly. It is especially suited to small
tools, server-driven interfaces, desktop utilities, and technical documents.

The deeper reason is architectural: pure Roc functions make views predictable,
while a selected platform gives the native host explicit control over I/O and
application capabilities. [Why Roc fits Rocci](/docs/concepts/why-roc/) covers that
design, including interpreted development and compiled delivery.

Continue with [installation](/docs/getting-started/installation/) or jump straight
to the [quickstart](/docs/getting-started/quickstart/).
